course: dictionary
lesson: 16078
title: Words that name a person by their job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words end in -wallah. A wallah is a person who does a certain job, or who is connected with a certain thing. The word comes from Hindi and Urdu, and you will hear it in Indian English. «The chai-wallah poured hot tea into little clay cups.» Chai means tea, so a chai-wallah is a tea seller.
explain: The first part of the word often tells you the job. «The dabbawala delivered my lunch in a neat metal box.» Dabba means box, so a dabbawala is a lunchbox delivery person. When you meet a new word, look for parts you already know, then check the sentence.
explain: British books from long ago used wallah too, but often as a joke. «Dad asked the computer wallah to fix the printer.» The computer wallah is the person in charge of computers. Some people find this old British use a little dated, so it is less common today.
fact: A wallah is a person who does a job or is connected with a thing.
fact: «Chai-wallah» means a tea seller.
fact: «Dabbawala» means a lunchbox delivery person.
fact: In old British slang, «wallah» is often used jokingly, as in «the computer wallah».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The chai-wallah poured hot tea into little clay cups.» What is a chai-wallah? | A kind of lunchbox | A train driver | *A tea seller | A computer expert in an office
exercise: In India, what does a dabbawala do? | Teaches music in a school | Sells newspapers on street corners | Repairs bicycles | *Delivers lunchboxes to people at work
exercise: «Dad asked the computer wallah to fix the printer.» In this sentence, what does computer wallah mean? | *A person in charge of computers, said jokingly | A new kind of computer game | A printer that makes a loud noise | A shop that sells paper
test: «The tech wallah at school showed us how to save our work.» What is a tech wallah? | A school bus driver | *A person in charge of technology, said jokingly | A student who is always late | A teacher who teaches maths
test: In chai-wallah, what does the word chai mean? | Bread | Sugar | *Tea | Rice
exam: Which languages does the word wallah come from? | *Hindi and Urdu | Welsh and Scots | French and German | Latin and Greek
